  "rules": "COLONEL BLOTTO - 100 soldiers, 5 equal fields. 2 players, simultaneous moves, 5 rounds.\n\nGOAL\nWin more rounds than your opponent.\n\nEACH ROUND\nThere are 5 battlefields, called F1 F2 F3 F4 F5 (in this order, left to right).\nAll battlefields are worth the same (1 point each).\nEvery round each player has exactly 100 soldiers to place (a fresh army each round).\nBoth players secretly choose how many soldiers to put on each battlefield, at the same time.\nThen both allocations are revealed. On each battlefield the player with MORE soldiers captures\nit; equal soldiers (including 0 vs 0) = nobody captures it.\nA round is won by the player who captures MORE battlefields. Equal numbers = the\nround is drawn (nobody wins it).\n\nEND AND SCORING\nAfter 5 rounds, the player who won more rounds wins the game. If rounds won are equal, the\nplayer who captured more battlefield points over the whole game wins; if that is equal too,\nthe game is a draw. Your score = rounds won. The game always lasts exactly 5 rounds (move cap).\n\nACTION FORMAT\nYour action is exactly 5 whole numbers >= 0 that add up to EXACTLY 100,\nlisted in battlefield order F1 to F5, separated by spaces (commas are also accepted).\nExamples: \"20 20 20 20 20\", \"35 35 30 0 0\", \"0 0 34 33 33\".\nWrong count of numbers, negative numbers, decimals, or a wrong total are illegal (first time: a\nwarning and the same turn again; second time: you lose the game). The legal-actions list is null\nbecause there are too many possible splits.\n\nWHAT YOU OBSERVE EACH TURN\nThe round number, this round's battlefield values, your soldiers,\nthe score in rounds and battlefield points, and the full history of earlier rounds (both\nallocations, who captured each battlefield, who won the round).",
